So I finally managed to ascend that character (what the heck, a dump
log follows).  The strategy worked as I outlined it.  Eventually I did
get crowned after I got enough divine protection that I stopped
worrying about my luck.  Mirrors didn't play a big role here.  Sokoban
was only 4 levels away from my altar, so I just used that all the
time.

The strategy was simple: Max out my luck, then go jump around in
Sokoban 7 times.  If at any time I got a spellbook, I would go jump in
Sokoban 3-4 times (not just 2 times, because sometimes my god would be
mollified in the intervening time and the first sacrifice when I got
back would increase my luck).  If, after a long time of sacrificing
and praying, I hadn't gotten additional divine prayer in awhile, I
figured my luck was too low, and I let a single clover through.

I never put away the blessed luckstone, and I was always very careful
to #pray immediately following a reconciliation message to avoid any
increases in luck.  I got something like 30 AC and 400 HP before I
voluntarily decided to get crowned, and there's no reason it couldn't
have gone on indefinitely.

Incidentally, playing illiterate was hell on earth.  I'm never doing
that again.  Going into it, I thought that lack of AC would be my
biggest problem, but divine protection easily solved that.  No, my
biggest problem was twofold: as a cavewoman, I couldn't twoweapon, and
without scrolls of enchant weapon, I couldn't do a lot of damage.
Dealing with certain monsters was painfully difficult.  I don't even
want to think about how many times my brain was eaten this past game.
Combine that with the lack of identification and ... ugh.

(Note that I picked up that Vorpal Blade on the Astral Plane.  Until
then, I had been using a combination of Excalibur, Fire Brand,
Demonbane, and Sunsword, depending on the situation.)



